## Latest-revision race schedule (required SQL tests — Gate 3, not executed here)

`LockLatestForUpdateAsync` ([`PoOrderRepository.cs`](../ErpWeb.Model/Repositories/Purchase/PoOrderRepository.cs) 136–149): unlocked `Max(PoRelNo)` then `UPDLOCK` that row. Concurrent `ReviseAsync` can insert `max+1` in the gap.

| # | Connection A | Connection B | Required outcome |
|---|--------------|--------------|------------------|
| R1 | GR post reads max=rev1, pauses before lock | PO revise commits rev2 | A must not post against rev1; fail “Purchase Order was revised. Reload and select the latest approved revision.”; **no** RecvQty/stock |
| R2 | PO revise holds header/applock | GR post waits then rechecks max | GR posts only latest approved rev or fails cleanly |
| R3 | GR draft saved with PoRelNo=1 | rev2 exists and is latest | Post rejects stale line `PoRelNo` (existing validator 4263+) **and** approval of rev1 must not authorize rev2 |
| R4 | GR post vs ForceClose/Cancel of latest | serialized on PO set lock | one winner; no partial batch |
| R5 | Multi-PO GR; one PO revises | sorted PoNo locks | all-or-nothing batch |
| R6 | Latest rev approved; older rev also had approval | GR for old RelNo | reject even if old instance APPROVED |

Existing cancelled-old-revision status is a **secondary** safeguard only; not a substitute for an atomic latest-revision contract.

---

## Policy / fingerprint / cutover (see DECISIONS file)

- `AssertGateAsync` 1087–1199: Pending first (blocks even if policy OFF); then policy OFF pass; then APPROVED/NOT_REQUIRED fingerprint (`null` fingerprint **passes** — V4-M1); then cutover exemption row; then progressed RecvQty/Received/Closed; then LegacyExempt insert; else fail submit-required.
- `SavePolicyAsync` CutoverAtUtc = `DateTime.UtcNow`. Document `CreatedDate` = company-local `_dates.Now` mapped to column `Created`. Comparison is Kind-unaware.
- Submit snapshots PolicyId, PolicyVersion, Gross/Taxes/Total, MaterialFingerprint, assignees (`SubmitLockedAsync` 1003–1024).

